From e7dd6a5c5e8ea0c595610cbba05058926a59c876 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:42:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patch 0167: OPTIONS in the title menu, JAPANESE CONTROLS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The title menu has a fifth row, OPTIONS, under BATTLE MODE. Its one row,
JAPANESE CONTROLS OFF / ON (confirm, left or right switch it; cancel goes back
with the cursor on OPTIONS), gives the game the Japanese disc's controls.

- The Japanese disc's code differs from the US one in three masks (input.h):
  ○ confirms, × cancels, △ is the third button. With the option on,
  CONFIRM_BUTTON, CANCEL_BUTTON and ALT_BUTTON read MOD_OPT_BUTTONS and are the
  Japanese ones; a button the code tests by its bit (△ opening the field menu)
  is the same on both discs and stays.
- The font draws each button glyph as the button that now does its job
  (modButtonGlyph at the three glyph lookups of font.c): "×Select △Cancel"
  reads "○Select ×Cancel" with no text of its own; a green △ (the fishing
  help's "submenu, under △") is the field menu's and stays. A glyph the text
  paints in its button's colour (× cyan 6, △ green 5, ○ orange 10) takes the
  colour of the button it now is (modButtonColor).
- The dialogue box's button (SYSTEM_W.TIM, three 16x12 frames, also the care
  menu's badge) becomes a ○ made from the disc's own × frames each time
  ETCTIM.BIN is uploaded: the cross painted over with the face, a ring drawn
  in its place in the PlayStation ○'s red, with a CLUT of its own (the frames'
  one with the two blues made red) in the page's filler at VRAM (352, 230),
  modButtonClut; with the option off the filler is put back.
- The option is saved (SAVE_TAG_OPTIONS 0x0009, u8[1]); a Continue takes it
  unless OPTIONS changed it since the console started. The title screen before
  a Continue always has the US controls.

